# Interface and configuration terminology

Use the native name to help people find a feature. Then explain what it means for their task. The English labels come from the frontend or official guidance we checked. A technical key with no editor label is marked as technical. We have not given it a made-up name.

This page covers frontend **20261028.5** and the official documentation checked on **12 November 2026**. The [native interface census](../reference/ha-interface-coverage.json) lists every route, panel and row. Not every screen is adapted by civica or visible to every account.

## Requests, conditions and evidence

“When”, “And if” and “Then do” are different parts of an automation. Selecting **Run actions** does not recreate the trigger. A condition result is a logical test, not a statement about every device.

Home Assistant’s [target-condition guidance](https://www.home-assistant.io/docs/automation/targets/#conditions-any-and-all) ignores unknown and unavailable targets for Any and All. An All condition can pass when every target is unknown or unavailable. Keep the result and the missing evidence apart.

