## Browse by task or type

<% register = JSON.parse(File.read(File.join(root, 'data', 'ha-terminology.json'))) %>
<% sources = register['sources'].to_h { |source| [source['id'], source] } %>
<% categories = [['automation-language','Automations and scripts'], ['dashboard-language','Dashboard interactions'], ['assist-language','Assist and voice'], ['security-language','Accounts and security'], ['energy-language','Energy and quantities'], ['installation-language','Installation and maintenance'], ['settings-labels','Exact Settings destination names'], ['view-types','View layouts'], ['card-types','Card names and keys'], ['card-features','Card feature names'], ['selector-types','Selector identifiers']] %>
<ul><% categories.each do |category,title| %><li><a href="#<%= escape(category) %>"><%= escape(title) %></a></li><% end %></ul>

<% categories.each do |category,title| %>
<h2 id="<%= escape(category) %>"><%= escape(title) %></h2>
<% if category == 'settings-labels' %><p>These are the named destinations in Settings. In another language, keep the translation Home Assistant shows. A destination may be hidden by permissions or by how Home Assistant is installed.</p><% end %>
<% if category == 'card-types' %><p>All 71 card keys. Some are internal, error, startup or old cards. A key being listed does not mean you can pick it in the editor.</p><% end %>
<% if category == 'card-features' %><p>All 53 feature keys. The card and entity decide which features appear. Do not invent an operation from a feature name.</p><% end %>
<% if category == 'selector-types' %><p>All 61 selector keys. The public blueprint documentation lists fewer. These keys name input types for configuration. Do not show them to a household as questions.</p><% end %>
<% register['terms'].select { |term| term['category'] == category }.sort_by { |term| term['native_name'].downcase }.each do |term| %>
<details class="civica-audit-detail" id="<%= escape(term['id'].downcase) %>">
<summary><strong><%= escape(term['native_name']) %></strong><% if term['code_identifiers'] %> — <code><%= escape(term['code_identifiers'].join(', ')) %></code><% end %></summary>
<% if term['native_name_kind'] %><p><strong>Name source:</strong> <%= escape(term['native_name_kind']) %>.</p><% end %>
<p><strong>Say:</strong> <%= escape(term['household_wording']) %><%= '.' unless term['household_wording'].end_with?('.') %></p>
<p><strong>What it means:</strong> <%= escape(term['first_use_explanation']) %></p>
<p><strong>Do not confuse it with:</strong> <%= escape(term['avoid_confusion']) %></p>
<% if term['code_kind'] %><p><strong>Kind of value:</strong> <%= escape(term['code_kind']) %>.</p><% end %>
<p>Reference: <code><%= escape(term['id']) %></code>. <% term['source_ids'].each_with_index do |source_id,index| %><%= ' · ' unless index.zero? %><a href="<%= escape(sources.fetch(source_id)['url']) %>"><%= escape(sources.fetch(source_id)['title']) %></a><% end %>.</p>
<% if term['native_label_pointer'] %><p><strong>Where the label comes from:</strong> <code><%= escape(term['native_label_pointer']) %></code>.</p><% end %>
</details>
<% end %>
<% end %>

## Check instructions against the installation

In the frontend we checked, **Tools** is where diagnostic tools are and **Apps** is the label for extra software. Older material says Developer tools or Add-ons, and Services instead of actions. Change a navigation instruction only after you check the real screen and version. Keep backend `service` fields, quotations and saved configuration as they are.

An English label may use US spelling, such as “Color”. Keep it when you name that control. Use “colour” in your own sentences. Do not change a native label to suit your spelling or make up a translation.

See [Home Assistant terminology](home-assistant-terminology.html) for what is covered and when it was checked. See the [compatibility register](../home-assistant/compatibility-register.html) before you say a feature works in a home.
